Title: LOW TIDE
Author: Vincent Marchetti
Draft date: June 2026

FADE IN:


INT. FISHING TRAWLER - WHEELHOUSE - NIGHT

Fog. CAPTAIN EDDIE MORAN, 50s, steers by radar alone. First mate CALLAHAN watches a blip trailing them port-side.
CALLAHAN
Coast Guard doesn't run dark on a night like this.
EDDIE
Then it's not Coast Guard.

EXT. TRAWLER DECK - NIGHT

Men in black climb from a rigid hull boat. Eddie nods — routine, ugly. Crates swap hands: fish out, shrink-wrapped bricks in.

INT. HARBOR OFFICE - NIGHT

DETECTIVE SARAH PELL, 40s, compares shipping logs to radar captures. Her partner, DUNN, sets down a PHOTO of Eddie's trawler.
PELL
Three runs this month. Same fog bank, same blind spot.
DUNN
Moran's been fishing these waters since we were in grade school.

INT. DOCKSIDE BAR - NIGHT

Pell slides onto a stool near Eddie. He doesn't look up from his beer.
PELL
Your manifest says cod. Your hull rides like heroin.
EDDIE
You come down here with proof or sympathy. I can't use either.

EXT. HARBOR - PREDAWN

Eddie's trawler pulls out. Pell watches from the pier, a warrant in her pocket she isn't ready to use.
PELL
One more run, Eddie. Then I stop asking nicely.

FADE OUT.


THE END
